@@title SQ-SHB Shipping Bin port (Farming for Blockheads), 2026-11-25 ([farming_for_blockheads.md](../farming_for_blockheads.md) 3.1, 5.1, 8, TODO `mod-integration #7`)
@@date 2026-11-25
@@jars creativedelight creativecommon
@@sources feature_writeup/farming_for_blockheads.md development/creativeDelight/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativedelight/farm/shippingbin kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/creativedelight/shipping_bin.js
@@text
@@text Not run. Built 2026-11-25. Needs `blockheads_upstream/farmingforblockheads-neoforge-26.3-26.3.0.2.jar` linked into srv/
@@text (every `*_upstream/` folder is). Bins at x 600 to 640, z 600, y -60 on the flat world; a stone roof at y -58 makes a
@@text bin "under a roof". Payout: 1 emerald per 128 points; values wheat 4, carrot 5 (rows 2.1).
@@table
## SQ-SHB-01 | Boot: donor jar verified, ids, recipes, payout table, axe tag
@group A
@commands Boot; `cdevtest reg item ^farmingforblockheads:`; `cdevtest recipes shipping_bin`; `cdevtest recipes courier_spawn`; `cdevtest tag block minecraft:mineable/axe`
@pass No "reads its textures" stop; items `shipping_bin` and `courier_spawn`; 12 `farmingforblockheads:shipping_bin` value rows and the two shaped recipes; no loot table error for `farmingforblockheads:gameplay/shipping_bin`; both blocks in the axe tag
@fails Donor jar missing or a wrong sha1 (stop with the message); `global.has('farmingforblockheads')` false (NCH skips every row: has.js `_modOf`); loot provider `shipment_value` not registered (table fails to parse)
bootreject reads its textures, models and recipes from the original Farming for Blockheads jar
bootreject Couldn't parse loot table farmingforblockheads
bootreject (Parsing error|Couldn't parse) .*farmingforblockheads
kjsreject shippingBin
> cdevtest reg item ^farmingforblockheads:
expect verb=reg kind=item regex=\S+ n=3
> cdevtest recipes shipping_bin/
expect verb=recipes id=creativedelight:shipping_bin/minecraft/wheat
expect verb=recipes id=creativedelight:shipping_bin/minecraft/sweet_berries
> cdevtest recipes shaped/courier_spawn
expect verb=recipes id=creativedelight:shaped/courier_spawn
> cdevtest tag block minecraft:mineable/axe
expect verb=tag kind=block tag=minecraft:mineable/axe .*farmingforblockheads:shipping_bin
expect verb=tag kind=block tag=minecraft:mineable/axe .*farmingforblockheads:courier_spawn

## SQ-SHB-02 | One load, partial sale and credit (SHB-03, SHB-04)
@group A
@commands Bin with 31 carrots (155 points) under open sky; 3 s; read the bin
@pass Slot 0 keeps 5 carrots, slot 6 holds 1 emerald, `Credit: 2`, `Value: 27`
@fails Every carrot taken (upstream B1 behavior); no emerald (payout table or `shipment_value` provider); credit 0
@absent farmingforblockheads:shipping_bin farmingforblockheads:courier_spawn farmingforblockheads:shipping_balloon farmingforblockheads:shipping_crate farmingforblockheads:courier (registered 2026-11-25, after the last /dumpall)
> forceload add 590 590 650 610
sleep 3
> setblock 600 -60 600 farmingforblockheads:shipping_bin[facing=north]{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:carrot",Count:31b}]}
sleep 4
> data get block 600 -60 600
expect has the following block data: .*Credit: 2
expect has the following block data: .*\{Count: 5b, Slot: 0b, id: "minecraft:carrot"\}|\{Slot: 0b, id: "minecraft:carrot", Count: 5b\}
expect has the following block data: .*minecraft:emerald

## SQ-SHB-03 | Below capacity and unsellable items stay (SHB-02, SHB-05)
@group A
@commands Bin with 31 wheat (124) and 8 cobblestone; 3 s; read it. Then add 1 wheat through a hopper above; 3 s; read it
@pass First read: no emerald, 31 wheat and the cobblestone in place; after the hopper adds 1 wheat: 1 emerald, no wheat left, cobblestone in its slot
@fails A sale below 128 points; the cobblestone taken; the hopper cannot insert (sided handler)
@absent farmingforblockheads:shipping_bin farmingforblockheads:courier_spawn farmingforblockheads:shipping_balloon farmingforblockheads:shipping_crate farmingforblockheads:courier (registered 2026-11-25, after the last /dumpall)
> setblock 604 -60 600 farmingforblockheads:shipping_bin[facing=north]{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:wheat",Count:31b},{Slot:1b,id:"minecraft:cobblestone",Count:8b}]}
sleep 3
> data get block 604 -60 600
# r1126q BF-FIX (2026-11-26): expect/reject read the whole row log, so the first read is pinned by its exact Items list (31 wheat, 8 cobblestone, no emerald) and the second by its own
expect has the following block data: .*Items: \[\{Slot: 0b, id: "minecraft:wheat", Count: 31b\}, \{Slot: 1b, id: "minecraft:cobblestone", Count: 8b\}\]
> setblock 604 -59 600 minecraft:hopper[facing=down]{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:wheat",Count:1b}]}
sleep 4
> data get block 604 -60 600
expect has the following block data: .*Items: \[\{Slot: 1b, id: "minecraft:cobblestone", Count: 8b\}, \{Slot: \d+b, id: "minecraft:emerald", Count: 1b\}\]

